  "raw_label": "postponed_or_procedural",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Vijendra Kumar Mishra vs State Of U.P. Thru. Addl. Chief Secy. ... on 21 August, 2024 Author: Rajesh Singh Chauhan Bench: Rajesh Singh Chauhan High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad, Lucknow Bench ?Neutral Citation No. - 2024:Ahc-Lko:56892 Court No. - 4 Case :- Writ - A No. - 6617 of 2024 Petitioner :- Vijendra Kumar Mishra Respondent :- State Of U.P. Thru. Addl. Chief Secy. Khadya Suraksha And Aushadhi Prashas Counsel for Petitioner :- Vijay Pathak,Rakesh Pathak Counsel for Respondent :- C.S.C. Hon'ble Rajesh Singh Chauhan,J. 1. Vijendra Kumar Mishra vs State Of U.P. Thru. Addl.",
    "facts": "Annexure No. 2 is a letter dated 03.08.2023 preferred by Assistant Commissioner, Food Safety And Drug Administration, Ayodhya to the Commissioner, Food Safety And Drug Administration, U.P., Lucknow apprising that the petitioner had foregone his promotion and requested to be posted at Ayodhya to look after his old aged father. Pursuant to the aforesaid development, the petitioner was not promoted on the post of Head Assistant and he was discharging his duties on the post of Senior Assistant at Ayodhya.",
    "arguments": "Learned Counsel for the petitioner has stated that the petitioner was promoted from the post of Senior Assistant to the post of Head Assistant on 25.07.2023 but on account of compelling family circumstances as his father is 80 years old and there is no one in the family to look after him, he had foregone his promotion making request that he may be permitted to serve on the post of Senior Assistant at his present place of posting i.e. Ayodhya. 5. Learned counsel for the petitioner has further submitted that immediately after the transfer order being passed on 30.06.2024, he preferred a representation dated 04.07.2024 (No.5) wherein he has categorically indicated that so as to meet out his extreme family conditions to take care of his old aged father, he had foregone his promotion, therefore, he may be permitted to be retained at Ayodhya. 6. 8. Be that as it may, if the petitioner had foregone his promotion on the post of Head Assistant to meet out his extreme family circumstances to look after his old aged father who is permanently residing at Ayodhya, unless there is any extreme administrative reason or any extreme administrative exigency to transfer the petitioner from Ayodhya, his bonafide grievance should have been considered by the competent authority i.e. Commissioner, Food Safety and Drug Vijendra Kumar Mishra vs State Of U.P. Thru. Addl. Chief Secy. ..."
  },
